From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:39:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Ring one compute doorbell per publish
 pass by default

Make g16_compute_onebell default 2: a publish pass rings the compute
pipe after its first compute record, so an idle firmware starts at once,
and once more when the pass ends if more records followed without a
doorbell. One firmware scheduler pass consumes every record up to the
queue head, so the per-record doorbells of a burst only added scheduler
passes.

On the J604 at depth 64, with the private notifier off, compute.light
took 36.05 us per command with 2 against 36.95 and 36.72 us with 0
before and after it (2.1 % less), and compute.heavy was unchanged
(557.79 against 558.41 and 557.91 us). Mode 1, one doorbell only at the
end of the pass, was 7.5 us slower and stays available for comparison.

Writing 0 restores one doorbell after each record.

RESULT: to be filled by the release owner

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 3976742e05..2c1d7d7219 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -490,8 +490,8 @@ pub(crate) fn onebell() -> u32 {
     "G16: doorbells of a render publication (default 0: one per pipe after its record; 1: both records, then the TA pipe only; 2: then the FS pipe only; 3: then both; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_compute_onebell` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static COMPUTE_ONEBELL: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_compute_onebell` (runtime 0644, default 2).
+static COMPUTE_ONEBELL: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(2);
 
 /// Doorbells of the compute publications of one publish pass, once the compute queue is
 /// registered. Each doorbell wakes one firmware scheduler pass, and one pass consumes every
@@ -512,7 +512,7 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_onebell() -> u32 {
     COMPUTE_ONEBELL_PARM,
     COMPUTE_ONEBELL,
     "g16_compute_onebell",
-    "G16: doorbells of the compute publications of one publish pass (default 0: one after each record; 1: one when the pass ends; 2: after the first record and when the pass ends; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: doorbells of the compute publications of one publish pass (default 2: after the first record and when the pass ends; 0: one after each record; 1: one when the pass ends; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 live_u32_param!(
